omment":""},{"DocComment":" This function will panic if the two slices have different lengths."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Copying two elements from a slice into another:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let src = [1, 2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":" let mut dst = [0, 0];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Because the slices have to be the same length,"},{"DocComment":" // we slice the source slice from four elements"},{"DocComment":" // to two. It will panic if we don't do this."},{"DocComment":" dst.copy_from_slice(&src[2..]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(src, [1, 2, 3, 4]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(dst, [3, 4]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Rust enforces that there can only be one mutable reference with no"},{"DocComment":" immutable references to a particular piece of data in a particular"},{"DocComment":" scope. Because of this, attempting to use `copy_from_slice` on a"},{"DocComment":" single slice will result in a compile failure:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```compile_fail"},{"DocComment":" let mut slice = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" slice[..2].copy_from_slice(&slice[3..]); // compile fail!"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" To work around this, we can use [`split_at_mut`] to create two distinct"},{"DocComment":" sub-slices from a slice:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut slice = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" {"},{"DocComment":"     let (left, right) = slice.split_at_mut(2);"},{"DocComment":"     left.copy_from_slice(&right[1..]);"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(slice, [4, 5, 3, 4, 5]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`clone_from_slice`]: slice::clone_from_slice"},{"DocComment":" [`split_at_mut`]: slice::split_at_mut"},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"Untagged":{"dat